WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.360
Test 2. This is the IELTS listening test. You will hear a number of different recordings

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:12.440
and you will have to answer questions on what you hear. There will be time for you to read

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:17.600
the instructions and questions and you will have a chance to check your work. All the

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:25.200
recordings will be played once only. The test is in four parts. At the end of the test you

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:32.400
will be given 10 minutes to transfer your answers to an answer sheet. Now turn to part

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:44.919
1. Part 1. You will hear a woman from a job agency giving information to a man about work

00:00:44.919 --> 00:00:51.240
in a chain of restaurants. First you have some time to look at questions 1 to 5.

00:01:15.919 --> 00:01:19.919
Now listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 5.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:30.120
So I understand you're interested in restaurant work. Yes, I've got a bit of experience and I

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:37.080
can provide references. That's good. I can check all that later. Now Milo's restaurants have some

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:42.599
vacancies at the moment. They're a really good company to work for. Lots of benefits. All right.

00:01:42.839 --> 00:01:49.320
Yes, they've got a very good reputation for looking after staff. For example, all employees

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:55.879
get training, even temporary staff. Oh really? That's quite unusual, isn't it? Certainly is.

00:01:55.879 --> 00:02:04.839
And do staff get free uniforms too? You just need to wear a white t-shirt and black trousers,

00:02:04.839 --> 00:02:11.479
it says here, so I guess not. But another benefit of working for a big company like this

00:02:11.479 --> 00:02:16.839
is that you can get a discount at any of their restaurants. Even at weekends? No,

00:02:16.839 --> 00:02:23.399
but you'll be working then anyway. Oh yes, I suppose so. Most of their restaurants are in

00:02:23.399 --> 00:02:30.600
the city centre, aren't they? So easy to get to by bus? Yes, that's right. But if you have to do

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:36.360
a late shift and finish work after midnight, the company will pay for you to get a taxi home.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:43.559
I probably won't need one. I think I'd use my bike. OK. Now they do have some quite specific

00:02:43.559 --> 00:02:49.160
requirements for the kind of person they're looking for. Milo's is a young, dynamic company

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:55.080
and they're really keen on creating a strong team. It's really important that you can fit in and get

00:02:55.080 --> 00:03:01.000
on well with everyone. Yep, I've got no problem with that. It sounds good actually. The last

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:06.919
place I worked for was quite demanding too. We had to make sure we gave a really high level

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:13.160
of service. That's good to hear because that will be equally important at Milo's. I know they want

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:18.839
people who have an eye for detail. That's fine. I'm very used to working in that kind of environment.

00:03:18.839 --> 00:03:24.119
Perfect. So the only other thing that's required is good communication skills,

00:03:24.119 --> 00:03:26.839
so you'll need to have a certificate in English. Sure.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:30.119
Before you hear the rest of the conversation,

00:03:30.119 --> 00:03:33.720
you have some time to look at questions 6 to 10.

00:03:56.839 --> 00:04:14.839
OK. Let's have a look at the current job vacancies at Milo's. The first one is in Wivenhoe Street.

00:04:15.399 --> 00:04:23.239
Sorry, where? Wivenhoe. W-I-V-E-N-H-O-E.

00:04:23.959 --> 00:04:27.160
It's quite central, just off Cork Street. Oh, right.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:31.320
They're looking for a breakfast supervisor. That would be OK.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:37.799
So you're probably familiar with the kind of responsibilities involved – obviously checking

00:04:37.799 --> 00:04:43.000
that all the portions are correct, etc. And then things like checking all the procedures

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:49.640
for cleaning the equipment are being followed. OK. And what about the salary? In my last job,

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:55.000
I was getting £9.50 per hour. I was hoping to get a bit more than that.

00:04:55.559 --> 00:05:03.880
Well, to begin with, you'd be getting £9.75, but that goes up to £11.25 after three months.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:07.799
That's not too bad. And I suppose it's a very early start.

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:14.200
That's the only unattractive thing about this job. But then you have the afternoons and evenings

00:05:15.079 --> 00:05:22.040
So the restaurant starts serving breakfast from 7am, and you'd have to be there at 5.30

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:25.399
to set everything up. But you'd be finished at 12.30.

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:29.079
Well, as you say, there are advantages to that.

00:05:29.799 --> 00:05:34.040
Now, you might also be interested in the job at the City Road branch.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:38.839
That's for a junior chef, so again a position of responsibility.

00:05:38.839 --> 00:05:43.720
I might prefer that, actually. Right. Well, obviously this role

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:49.480
would involve supporting the sous-chef and other senior staff. And you'd be responsible

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:54.519
for making sure there's enough stock each week, and sorting out all the deliveries.

00:05:54.519 --> 00:06:00.359
I've never done that before, but I imagine it's fairly straightforward once you get the hang of it.

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:05.160
Yes, and you'd be working alongside more experienced staff to begin with,

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:09.799
so I'm sure it wouldn't be a problem. The salary's slightly higher here.

00:06:09.799 --> 00:06:13.640
It's an annual salary of £23,000. Right.

00:06:14.359 --> 00:06:19.000
I know that if they like you, it's likely you'll be promoted quite quickly,

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:22.519
so that's worth thinking about. Yes, it does sound interesting.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:27.480
What are the hours like? The usual, I think. There's a lot of

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:33.959
evening and weekend work, but they're closed on Mondays. But you do get one Sunday off every

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:37.720
four weeks. So, would you like me to send off your CV?

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:51.720
That is the end of part one. You now have one minute to check your answers to part one.

00:07:03.959 --> 00:07:05.000
Thank you.

00:07:33.959 --> 00:07:34.459
Thank you.

